{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneralRankQuadratic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneralRankQuadratic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Coxeter.Length"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.channel_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.channel_minus","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeGeneralRankQuadratic.lean#L119-L140","doc":"**The e₋ channel at every rank**: for `h = q − q⁻¹`, the vector\n`Mv − q·v` is a `(−q⁻¹)`-eigenvector direction of the generator action —\nthe antisymmetric channel. Together with `channel_plus` this constructs, at\nEVERY rank, exactly the channel pair the archimedean τ-functor must send to\n`(H^{1,0}, H^{0,1})` (forced shadow #3960; B1 dictionary #3955). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.channel_plus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.channel_plus","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeGeneralRankQuadratic.lean#L103-L117","doc":"**The e₊ channel at every rank**: for `h = q − q⁻¹`, the vector\n`Mv + q⁻¹·v` is a `q`-eigenvector direction of the generator action — the\nsymmetric channel. Derived from the quadratic by pure algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.mulSimple_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.mulSimple_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeGeneralRankQuadratic.lean#L74-L97","doc":"**The Hecke quadratic at EVERY rank**: `σᵢ² = h·σᵢ + 1` as an operator\nidentity on the length-rule module of an arbitrary Coxeter system. The two\ncases are exactly the ±1 length toggle (`length_mul_simple`); the involution\n`u·sᵢ·sᵢ = u` is `simple_mul_simple_self`. Specializing `W` to a symmetric\ngroup discharges the `hecke_quadratic` field content of\n`HeckeBraidedPresentation` at the action level for all n simultaneously —\npreviously known only concretely at n = 2, 3, 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.mulSimple_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.mulSimple_smul","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeGeneralRankQuadratic.lean#L67-L72","doc":"`mulSimple` is R-homogeneous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.mulSimple_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.mulSimple_add","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeGeneralRankQuadratic.lean#L60-L65","doc":"`mulSimple` is additive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.mulSimple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.mulSimple","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeGeneralRankQuadratic.lean#L50-L58","doc":"Right action of the Hecke generator `T_{sᵢ}` on the function module\n`W → R`, by the exact Iwahori–Hecke length rule (coefficient form): the\ncoefficient at `u` after acting is `v(u·sᵢ)` plus `h·v(u)` exactly when\n`sᵢ` is a right descent of `u`. Specialized to `W = Sₙ` this reproduces the\nconcrete `mulσ` tables of `HeckeH3AlgebraLaws` / `HeckeH4StabilizationRung`\nentry-for-entry. ","signatureChunk":0}]}